From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:00:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] wasmtime: schedule epoch polling through bounded fuel
 refills

Add an engine-owned polling interval that reuses fuel refills for private
entry and loop checks. Preserve native and escaping entry, startup,
host-return and rooted exception-continuation checks, callback yields,
interruptions and exact fuel accounting. Reject unsupported execution
modes rather than accepting incomplete continuation coverage.

Retain register-preserving metering handlers and their GC stack-map
support. Reload authoritative fuel on caught exceptions so unwinding
cannot restore stale caller charges.

Keep zero-interval engine metadata and compatibility hash inputs identical
to the pinned upstream representation. Encode nonzero intervals in a
separate versioned metadata extension and reject mismatched intervals.
This permits independent compatible upgrades while older runtimes reject
artifacts that rely on the new runtime polling contract.

Sixteen focused metering and artifact tests pass with both null and moving
copying collectors. Cross-version probes execute legacy and new zero-mode
artifacts in both directions with matching output and fuel, compare exact
metadata and hash inputs, and verify old-runtime rejection of polling
artifacts even with module version-string checks disabled.
